A1. This is the time when, dressed in her mo(u)rning clothes, she offered a toast to her late husband, who was buried in a newspaper. ~ BREAKFAST
A9. Bills! Bills! Bills! and all for feeding the younger generation. ~ BEAKS
A10. This came from Mobile. ~ AUTO
A11. To leak gas. ~ ORATE
A12. The way the new bathing suits look. ~ TINY
A13. There is very little volume to this (abbr.). ~ DL
A15. A saxophone solo. ~ BLARE
A16. What they did with the relief for the unemployed. ~ SENT
A17. A router's by-word. ~ VIA
A18. It is great to be this when the skies are blue. ~ ALIVE
A19. Even a little tiff like this might result in the overthrow of China. ~ SPAT
A20. Where all the perusers come from. ~ PERU
A21. What Amos 'n Andy seem to be among the radio fans. ~ FAVORITES
A23. Let peace do this and all will be well. ~ REIGN
A24. Sis made a thesis from this little article. ~ THE
A25. An interview with Gandhi's goat. ~ MAA
A26. Scrammed for a living. ~ EARNED
A27. The cop that protects all of those musical gems. ~ COPYRIGHT
A30. What the presidential campaign does every four years. ~ RECURS
A33. The only thing belonging to the cow that the packers have not utilized. ~ MOO
A34. This has great ambitions to be a flier. ~ BEE
A36. Scratched for a living. ~ WROTE
A37. These are not as black as they are painted. ~ MINSTRELS
A40. What the Chinese have up their sleeves now. ~ ARMS
A41. There were 4 of these at the ball game and two of them were in silk stockings. ~ RUNS
A42. What it does "down by the winegar works." ~ REEKS
A43. It is a crime to do this. ~ ROB
A44. If thou art going to make a will, thou hadst better use this form. ~ WILT
A45. Here is a chance to make some money. ~ CENTS
A46. This will keep you in good health and spirits (abbr.). ~ DR
A47. What the raccoon has contributed to college sports ~ HIDE
A48. The talk of the town (plur.). ~ CHATS
A49. This wife is always a nag. ~ MARE
A50. What the doctor does for his fee these days. ~ WAITS
A51. General Dawes always carries his extra pipe in a case of this. ~ EMERGENCY

D1. The man who carries the bag. ~ BEARER
D2. This is something of interest. ~ RATE
D3. Skimp and save for a living. ~ EKE
D4. A Roman coin that originally weighed one pound. (The Romans never hoarded their money. Now we know why.) ~ AS
D5. What we might fall into if we saw Dame Prosperity parked around the corner. ~ FAINT
D6. One reason why children are spoiled. ~ AUNT
D7. A litter airy home. ~ STY
D8. The entrance and exit of Toronto. ~ TO
D9. What we would like to say to the one who wins a fight with a road map and puts it in its proper fold. ~ BRAVO
D11. A branch that should be popular in Geneva. ~ OLIVE
D12. What has been brewing in China (plur.). ~ TEAS
D13. Slow music. ~ DIRGE
D14. A woman who knows how to wear clothes. ~ LAUNDRESS
D15. Applesauce. ~ BLAH
D16. By Gum! This is a good flavor to choose. ~ SPEARMINT
D17. When there is any trouble, this one always takes it to heart. ~ VEIN
D18. The time one thinks up clever repartee. ~ AFTERWARD
D19. Stick around for a while. ~ STAY
D20. The kind of a miss she made. ~ PERT
D22. Pesky little creatures of darkness. ~ IMPS
D23. Several like this will make any collegiate yell. ~ RAH
D26. Me, myself and I. ~ EGOS
D27. Have you received yours yet? Everyone is getting them. ~ CUTS
D28. Since this has come from the underworld it has been refined and polished. ~ ORE
D29. After scientific research we have discovered these electrified particles come from onions. ~ IONS
D31. "What is wrong here?" ~ ERROR
D32. What a cock-eyed rooster tries to "high hat" it with. ~ COMB
D34. A red in the vegetable kingdom (plur.). ~ BEETS
D35. Men are always hunting for these. ~ ELKS
D37. If any obstinate man is listening in perhaps he realizes that his wife married something like this. ~ MULE
D38. When this compact was broken there was a lot of powder spilled. ~ TREATY
D39. The only things that can be raised in the cities. ~ RENTS
D41. What was put up on the race horse. ~ RIDER
D44. They always try to put things over on this conductor. ~ WIRE
D45. The attractive part of Chicago. ~ CHIC
D47. If you make this a Swift one, you may get a premium. ~ HAM
D48. They are even trying to make a racket out of this. ~ CAN
D49. A personal objective. ~ ME
D50. This couple always keeps the score. ~ WE


